    "total_efficiency_score": 791.29,
    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is anchored today by **Lawrence Butler**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 74.61 as he leads off against Singer. The combination of an elevated batting order position and a significant 13% boost from his dynamic platoon profile makes **Lawrence Butler** our primary engine for runs. He is closely followed by **Bryce Harper**, whose 71.32 score against Palmquist remains elite despite the platoon disadvantage, supported by a strong .387 xwOBA. We are also high on **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.91) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52); **Dylan Beavers** benefits immensely from a 16% park factor bump and a favorable matchup against Rodriguez, while **Geraldo Perdomo** draws a highly exploitable 4.92 xERA from V\u00e1squez. Both players provide the speed-first profile we prioritize to maintain our edge in the scarcest 5x5 category.\n\nThe toughest decision at the back of the bench was leaving **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.99) on the pine. While **Jung Hoo Lee** received a subtle boost for his ability to swipe bags against a slower-to-the-plate Gore, his efficiency was capped by a difficult platoon matchup and a lower raw base projection compared to **Gavin Sheets** and **JJ Bleday**. Risk management remains a theme for today: **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Gavin Sheets** are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" meaning we are operating on assumed batting orders. Should either be bumped down the order, their efficiency scores will contract accordingly. We are intentionally limiting exposure to **Masyn Winn** today, as his score of 44.65 barely exceeds the floor; his matchup against Weathers\u2014a pitcher with a sub-3.50 xERA\u2014significantly suppresses his upside, and we are only deploying him to maximize game caps while sacrificing some potential efficiency.",
